 ## Build layer
 
 Built in the `adapters` Crane artifact layer; the layer compiles all adapters in one Cargo invocation, so they build concurrently.
+
+## Isolated legacy snapshot
+
+The local candidate adds `codex legacy-snapshot --json --offline`.
+It returns daily and session reports from one strict capture.
+The envelope includes `historyMode: "legacy"`.
+Ordinary reports retain the parent routing and session selectors.
+
+The strict command uses the first recorded thread ID and compares complete decoded streams.
+Equal streams and exact prefixes select one longest capture.
+Missing identity, conflicting streams, duplicate keys, lineage, replay, and incomplete counters refuse.
+Session rows use recorded thread IDs. No account identity is inferred.
+
+This command remains a synthetic Linux experiment. It does not establish legacy producer support.
+Last-only counters, total-only counters, and omitted reasoning counts remain unsupported in the strict command.
+Unrelated `.zst` files and unused large or deeply nested JSON values can also cause refusal.
+Production adoption still needs source qualification, stored-session migration, performance checks, and native acceptance.
